    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1224">

                <pb facs="0995" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2906.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-26T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 25, 7 p.m. I learn at the Foreign Office that orders have been sent
                    to the commander of the forces at Ciudad Juárez to <pb facs="0996" n="880"
                        xml:id="pg880"/> engage the revolutionary forces at a point about 13 miles
                    distant from the city, and under no circumstances to make a resistance in Ciudad
                    Juárez. These instructions have also been communicated to the Mexican consul at
                    El Paso.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
